 {:seon.task/name "teaching-is-data"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-06 at cb1b5bfa46 and three changes to it, six tasks, one run each, deepseek-flash, cap 40 (replies with text; tasks that reached green; a difference of a task or two means little, breadth merged for the first time in the last arm and vars-history, merged in the others, capped there). Main as merged: 0 of 197; 2 of 6. The inserted eval's intent as its text: 16 of 239; 1 of 6, contaminated by a stale recording. And :turn \"N of 40\" on each answer: 38 of 221; 1 of 6. And the page speaking at each tenth turn: 21 of 190; 1 of 6, plus one closed when its deferred tests errored at the gate (seon.reconcile/a-gate-that-cannot-run-its-tests-tells-the-agent). Kept: the first two (cheap, true, no eval). Dropped: the tenth-turn line, no effect shown. Earlier controls with a page message leading each turn had text on 74% of calls and merged 3 of 24, so text alone does not merge tasks. First writes at turns 36-38 in many runs, in the agents' words: `I have 5 turns left, so I'll go straight to the fix`: they read until told time is passing. Repeats cost most: vars-history ran one form 24 times at 17,000 tokens a turn (7.5M tokens). No fix for reading or repeating is shown yet. An agent writes no text: 0 of 9 replies held text on the merged reconcile run (2026-11-06, render-evals), though the system message asks for it and seon.render/the-render-is-an-eval's plan asked a live session to still write text. The person's chat reads nothing but evals; what teaches it, and does the first eval being Seon's suppress it? A third real run (2026-11-06, reconcile on render-evals): the proof written at turn 5 and three functions fixed, then the same form 17 times from turn 24 to its cap, each answered by :again. An identical repeat is the biggest loss measured. A second real run (2026-11-06, reconcile on render-evals): the fix written by turn 7 and every proof green at turn 9, then 31 turns reading seon.cost because the status said `red test that is no proof`, a test the agent could not act on. A red that is not the agent's says whose it is and what the agent does: message root, or stop reading. A real run to answer (2026-11-05, long-string on render-speaks, cap 40, 693k tokens): 39 evals of reading, one `source` a turn, no proof written, the last five the same form, each told by :again to run something else. The status names the proof to write from the first request. What in the page makes an agent write the proof and try something before it has read everything? The owner, 2026-11-05: the agent's entity \"teaches them about the system, it explain what task they are working on, how messaging works when they get a message, evertyhing. It's all data driven\"; \"NO SPECIAL CASE FOR CITING\"; \"NO OTHER MECHANISMS\". What an agent reads is an eval whose result is useful or data on its entity drawn by a render. docs/prompt.md moves to data an agent's pull holds, drawn by a render, and evals at its opening, with seon.model/eval-tool's descriptions reduced to its shape; session-open and the example session tags go; a message's render says how messaging works; root's stage messages and how a kind is worked become data. Citing has no writer of its own: seon.render.ui/page-cites, seon.task/agent-cites-tx, :seon.config.agent/cites, my.agent/cite! and uncite! go for ordinary data and swap!. An eval's answer holds its value: :again, :helper-shadowed, the uncontracted finding and its fix, and main-line become data on the agent, drawn, or go. Also traces what the first pass left: seon.learn, seon.ctx.search/relevance, seon.ctx.wire/help-text. Agents' own renders are taught here: a key of its own and a render (docs/ctx.md#adding-a-datum-and-its-render). Proofs: two agents with different data read different context with no code changed; the words of the wire's system message come from the entity."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
